<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Ramaphosa joins SAfrica's JSE as committee member.</title>
<headline>Ramaphosa joins SAfrica's JSE as committee member.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cyril Ramaphosa, South Africa's union leader turned top-flight businessman, has joined the Johannesburg Stock Exchange Committee as a non-stockbroker member, the bourse said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Ramaphosa has several high-profile board positions in the South African business community, including deputy-chairman of New Africa Investment Ltd and chairman of Johnnic.</p>
<p>He also holds directorships at First National Bank, Metropolitan Life and South African Breweries.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
